# The sensorext binary now uses stock's hal_graphics_composer_default_exec label
# (see file_contexts), so the bespoke vendor_hal_sensorext DOMAIN is gone. The
# SERVICE type stays in service.te, because service_contexts still maps
# motorola.hardware.sensors.ISensorExt/default to it and that avoids stock's
# hal_graphics_composer_service, which trips AOSP's
# hal_attribute_service(hal_graphics_composer, ...) neverallow.
allow hal_sensors_default vendor_hal_sensorext_service:service_manager find;
allow hal_graphics_composer_default vendor_hal_sensorext_service:service_manager add;

# ...and finding it is not enough. `find` only gets the multihal a binder HANDLE
# from servicemanager; the first thing libbinder does with it is send an
# INTERFACE_TRANSACTION to read the interface descriptor, and that is a binder
# CALL into the sensorext process -- which runs as hal_graphics_composer_default,
# because its binary carries hal_graphics_composer_default_exec (see
# file_contexts). Without this rule that transaction is denied 104 times:
#
#   avc: denied { call } scontext=u:r:hal_sensors_default:s0
#        tcontext=u:r:hal_graphics_composer_default:s0 tclass=binder
#
# so getInterfaceDescriptor() returns "" and the multihal fails:
#
#   E ...multihal: associateClass: Expecting binder to have class
#     'motorola.hardware.sensors.ISensorExt' but descriptor is actually ''.
#
# The ISensorExt proxy is then NULL and sensors.qsh.so dereferences it in
# ambient_light_alt::ambient_light_alt() -> SIGSEGV, 23 times, so the multihal
# never registers and the device has NO SENSORS AT ALL.
#
# That is also why the UI is stuck on the cover panel. device_state_configuration.xml
# keys every fold posture on com.motorola.sensor.hinge_posture, so with no sensors:
#   E DeviceStateProviderImpl: Failed to find Sensor with type:
#       com.motorola.sensor.hinge_posture and name: Hinge Posture  Wakeup
#   E DeviceStateManagerService: Cannot notify device state info change before
#       the initial state has been committed.
# DeviceStateManagerService never commits an initial posture, so the framework
# never switches to the inner display. It was never a mirroring problem, which is
# why config_localDisplaysMirrorContent=false (arcfox bcfacb9) did not help.
#
# NOTE this supersedes the older "sensorext SIGABRT in SensorExt::initAlsComp"
# theory, which is FALSIFIED: vendor.moto_sensorext starts exactly once (pid 2338
# in bc20), never aborts and never restarts. It is alive the whole time; the
# caller simply cannot talk to it.
#
# No neverallow blocks this: AOSP only neverallows ADDING
# hal_graphics_composer_service/_hwservice (already avoided by using our own
# vendor_hal_sensorext_service type above) and hal_graphics_composer_server fork.
binder_call(hal_sensors_default, hal_graphics_composer_default)
